<h2>Why Landscape Lighting Systems Fail in Austin</h2>
<p>Landscape lighting lives in a hard environment. It is buried in alkaline caliche soil, soaked by irrigation every morning, baked at 140 degrees on a July afternoon, chewed by string trimmers, dug up by dogs and buried under live oak leaf litter twice a year. Even well-built systems need attention, and systems built with aluminum fixtures and pierce-style connectors start failing within a few seasons. Landscape lighting repair Austin homeowners call us for almost always traces back to one of a handful of causes:</p>
